Most likely issue: the value is not exactly "Reinvestment Director" anymore.

Your code does this exact comparison:

df["DIRECTOR_ROLE__C"] == "Reinvestment Director"

That fails if Salesforce/Dataiku now has:

reinvestment director
Reinvestment Director 
REINVESTMENT DIRECTOR
Reinvestment Director   # hidden non-breaking space

Fix it by normalizing the field like you did for TYPE:

role = (
    df["DIRECTOR_ROLE__C"]
    .fillna("")
    .astype(str)
    .str.replace("\u00A0", " ", regex=False)
    .str.strip()
    .str.upper()
)
director_c = df["DIRECTOR__C"].fillna("").astype(str).str.strip()
df["Director"] = np.where(
    role.eq("REINVESTMENT DIRECTOR"),
    "IRM Assigned",
    np.where(
        director_c.eq(""),
        "Other",
        df["DIRECTOR__C"]
    )
)

